description.narrative:
The project has demonstrated significant progress across all components, with several results already exceeding 2026-2028 targets:

Public Procurement - Horizontal Criteria

- 3,244 green procurement procedures in 2024 (6.91%), surpassing 2026 target (2,000);

- 344 social procurement procedures (target 2026: 109);

- 16 trainings on horizontal criteria (410 participants);

- Mentoring support provided to major contracting authorities to apply green and social criteria (e.g. Ministry of Agriculture, Ministry of Environmental Protection, Environmental Protection Agency, Clinical Center of Serbia);
three green/two social procurement procedures completed with NALED support;

- Tender documentation models for green and social criteria prepared and tested.

Public Procurement - Innovation Procurement

- Training of Trainers conducted (13 participants);

- National trainings for contracting authorities launched (31 participants in the first session; further sessions scheduled);

- Analysis of Scientific Research Organizations' (SRO) procurement challenges completed; four trainings for SRO delivered (86 participants). A guide and internal procedures for SRO procurement are under preparation.

Competition & Procurement Integrity

- Analysis of the role of the Commission for the Protection of Competition (CPC) with recommendations completed;

- 2 CPC trainings on detecting competition infringements; Cooperation between CPC and Public Procurement Office (PPO) strengthened through roundtables;

- Comparative analysis of EU practices on increasing competition prepared;

- 7 trainings on procurement techniques and instruments (224 participants);

- Draft competition modules prepared for the e-Learning platform.

Procurement System Oversight (PPO, Republic Commission, Budget Inspection)

- PPO website redesigned and launched; staff trained; several guides updated, including the Guide on Green Public Procurement.

Analyses delivered:

- Public Procurement Portal functionality,
- EU alignment of the Law on Public Procurement,
- Green/social procurement 2020 - 2024.

Republic Commission: financial management and control system updated, risk management strategy prepared; database security improved; staff retreat to improve communication skills  IT training delivered.

Budget Inspection: Analysis of the position and state of the Budget Inspection in the field of public procurement completed; workshops on framework agreement technique and conclusion of contracts delivered (37 participants).

Bidders - Competitiveness & Capacity

- 11 dedicated bidder trainings delivered; 381 participants.

- Tailored training program developed based on needs analysis. The analysis identified priority sectors: maintenance & repair, hygiene & cleaning, engineering, architecture, design, technical services, and construction

Tools for bidders:

- e-Learning platform (www.lppp.rs) expanded; 3,000 registered users. New tender models, guides and analyses uploaded regularly. Competition modules under review for publication.

Behavioural change/perceptions:

- Strong rise in bidder support for qualitybased award criteria (from 60%  78%)

- Platform feedback indicates high usability and improved bidder confidence.

NGOs & Media

- 3 media trainings delivered (33 participants),

- First public procurement perception survey completed, showing declining trust among the citizens in fairness and transparency, high perception of corruption among the citizens (83%), but also strong support by bidders for more use of quality-based criteria.

ESG & Regenerative Agriculture, Energy

ESG Hub:

- ESG Hub: strategic framework  feasibility study completed; operational planning underway;

- ESG workshops held, promotional campaign ongoing (3 podcasts, strong media traction);

Supply chains:

- Crop husbandry supply chain sustainability analysis disseminated; Wood supply chain sustainability analysis completed; guide and training delivered; two additional supply chains identified for analysis;

Regenerative agriculture:

- Regenerative agriculture guide produced and distributed nationwide; roundtables held; nutritional analysis underway; reform proposals included in Grey Book 17 and presented at CORE Days; Regenerative Agricultual District (RAD) conceptualization initiated (mapping, institutional readiness, policy frameworks).

Energy transition:

- Sustainable Energy Council established; three sessions held;

- Power Purchase Agreement (PPA) analysis completed; roadmap for pilot corporate PPA prepared.

Social entrepreneurship:

- Social Entrepreneurship Hub established and operational (promotion, networking, cooperation with local government units, database of social enterprises in Serbia underway);

- Promotional campaign launched;

- Advocacy for the adoption of Social Entrepreneurship Development Program ongoing.

PublicPrivate Dialogue (PPD)

- 25 Alliance meetings held across four Alliances;

- Active involvement in reforms (property, environment, food/agriculture, e-Government).

Regulatory Reform & Evidence Base:

- 27 analyses/statistics/indexes produced (target: 25);

- Regulatory Index of Serbia (RIS) 2025 published (methodology expanded), showing a sharp decline - the largest drop in five years - driven by poor legislative planning, major delays in bylaws, weakened transparency, and significantly reduced public consultations;

- Grey Book 17 published; Grey Book 18 underway; 

- Local e-Government Index (LEI) methodology revised; software and website updated.
